  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, events <math><mi>A</mi><mi>,</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math><mi>C</mi></math> are mutually exclusive and exhaustive, hence <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
